    "explanation": "Both parties read the numbers the same way, and the tribunal agrees: this trip deviated, and a partial refund of SGD 0.60 is due to the rider.\n\nDeviation (POL-RD-01). The governing measurement is the GPS trace, not the rounded copy on the trip record. The trace records 4.05 km (EV-GPS-02846); the booked optimal route was 3.2 km (EV-TRIP-02846); the excess is 0.85 km, which is 26.56% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires both establishment tests to pass, and both do: more than 20% of optimal, and more than 0.8 km absolute. The policy's trace-governs rule matters here — the trip record's own copy, actual_distance_km 4.00 km, would give an excess of exactly 0.80 km and would fail the absolute limb. Because POL-RD-01 says the trace figure governs, the deviation stands at 0.85 km. The excess is below 50% and below 8.0 km, so it is not a MATERIAL deviation and the POL-RD-06 repeat-pattern check is not engaged (nothing turns on this, as the profile check comes out the same way).\n\nTrace integrity (POL-RD-07). The trace has 37 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds. It is not impaired under limbs (a) to (c), so the deviation may be established on the trace alone and needs no independent corroboration.\n\nExcuses (POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-12, POL-RD-08). The chat log is empty — 0 messages, EV-CHAT-02846 — so there is no rider-requested detour and no rider-supplied address change. The trip record shows pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at both null and amended_optimal_distance_km null, so POL-RD-05 cannot be run. The vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The driver's answer, 'Followed the app.', cites no evidence ID and points to no traffic advisory, no chat instruction, no amendment and no pooled itinerary; under POL-RD-08 an assertion that cites no evidence carries no weight and the driver's burden is not discharged. No exculpatory clause is available.\n\nRefund arithmetic (POL-RD-02; fare model METERED, and the surge multiplier is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier = 1.0). recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 3.2 + 0.28 x 6.0) x 1.0) + 0.80 platform fee = (3.80 + 2.40 + 1.68) + 0.80 = 8.68. Charged_total = 9.28. Refund = 9.28 - 8.68 = 0.60. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and is 6.47% of charged_total, far below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 0.60, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05.\n\nPass-through lines (POL-RD-09). The fare breakdown carries zero ERP gantries, zero tolls and no airport surcharge, so there is no off-route or phantom line to correct and nothing may be added on top of the 0.60.\n\nProfiles. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d 398, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift applies and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0, so the POL-RD-08 extra-corroboration rule is not engaged. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter and the other profile fields are context only under POL-GEN-01 and were not used as grounds. Two claims in the audit record that cited the missing advisory artifact without naming its issue code were discarded on the referee's mechanical check and were not relied on.\n\nConfidence. The finding rests on the GPS trace and the trip record, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor.\n\nExecution. The monetary effect, SGD 0.60, does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so this provisional ruling is executed automatically. It was made without human review, and either party may appeal within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
